What is the role of Hashing and Salt in securing passwords ?
=====================================================
→Purpose of hashing and salt is to make secure the password
Role of Hashing in Securing Passwords
Hashing converts a password into a fixed-length unreadable value.
It is a one-way process (cannot be reversed)
Original password cannot be retrieved
Even developers or admins cannot see real passwords
👉 If the database is leaked, attackers only get hashed values, not passwords.
Example:
 password123 → $2b$10$K8f9...

Role of Salt in Securing Passwords
Salt is a random value added to the password before hashing.
Same passwords get different hashes
Protects against rainbow table attacks
Stops attackers from guessing passwords in bulk


👉 Even if two users have the same password, their stored hashes will be different.
 Hashing + Salt Together (How It Works)
User enters a password
System generates a random salt
Password + salt are hashed together
Only the hash + salt are stored in the database
 How can we create Hash passwords in Node js?
===========================================
const crypto = require("crypto");
function hashAndSaltPassword(password) {
  // 1️⃣ Generate random salt
  const salt = crypto.randomBytes(16).toString("hex");
  // 2️⃣ Create hash using SHA-256
  const hash = crypto.createHash("sha256");
  // 3️⃣ Update hash with salt + password
  hash.update(salt + password);
  // 4️⃣ Convert hash to hex string
  const hashedPassword = hash.digest("hex");
  // 5️⃣ Return as single string (salt:hash)
  return `${salt}:${hashedPassword}`;
}
// Example usage
const storedPassword = hashAndSaltPassword("mypassword123");
console.log(storedPassword);
